# The base's pad pressure in CHROMATIC mode: a held pad's poly pressure goes out on the note its note on
# sent (stock: 24 semitones above it, and moved by UP or DOWN during the hold), and none after its note
# off. After a boot BD plays note 36 (0x24) on CHRO's pads. Needs PAD DEST and PRESSURE DST sending to USB.
# Then a roll with RTRG held: the base sends its pressure on the played note too (stock: none).
# Enters CHROMATIC with CHRO and leaves it with CHRO (the screen does not change: a pad's note shows it). Leaves BD's aftertouch at 0.
name: pad-pressure-chromatic
state: changes

key CHRO
wait 500
midi held begin
pad BD down 100
wait 300
pad BD pressure 60
wait 300
key UP
wait 300
pad BD pressure 30
wait 300
pad BD up
wait 300
pad BD pressure 20
wait 300
midi held end
key DOWN                            # back to the layout BD plays 36 on
wait 300
hold RTRG
wait 300
midi roll begin
pad BD down 100
wait 300
pad BD pressure 60
wait 500
mem at60 0x800067de 2
pad BD pressure 0
pad BD up
wait 300
midi roll end
release RTRG
wait 300
key CHRO
wait 500
midi out begin                      # CHRO again: the pads' own notes, not CHROMATIC's 36
pad BD down 100
wait 300
pad BD up
wait 300
midi out end
expect held has note 36
expect held has polyat 36 30
expect held has polyat 36 15
expect held lacks polyat 60
expect held lacks polyat 64
expect held lacks polyat 36 10
expect held.polyat == 2
expect roll has polyat 36 30
expect at60 == 1e00
expect out.notes == 1
expect out lacks note 36
